  "id": "COMPOUND:42909 - PROTEIN:6138",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex but consistent pathway linking cholesta-5,7,8(14),22E-tetraen-3-one to the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14. This compound appears to act as a target for Caspase-5, which in turn is targeted by two distinct compounds, both of which ultimately interact with the proteasome subunit. The shared involvement of Caspase-5 and the proteasome subunit in this chain of targets implies a potential role for cholesta-5,7,8(14),22E-tetraen-3-one in modulating proteasome activity through Caspase-5. The evidence supports a mechanism where the compound may influence proteasome function via Caspase-5, potentially affecting protein degradation pathways. The presence of multiple target compounds that converge on the proteasome subunit suggests a broader regulatory role, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
